35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"The survey shows daylight was the top complaint, yet the plan ignores it. I worry we are repeating past mistakes.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The plan is flawed. It ignores the survey’s top complaint. We must not repeat the chaos of the past year’s shuffles.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I found the billing is based on area, not people. We pay for empty desks. Plus, moving costs 6,200 yen each time.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mio,,"@Daisuke, six thousand yen per move? That’s steep! But my badge data shows we arrive at wildly different times. We can’t just assume everyone’s there at eight!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Nine decibels louder by the printer. That’s a constant headache. Plus, chairs take days to settle. We need a quiet, stable spot.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, your timing data is helpful. I hope we can arrange desks so neighbors are present when we need them, not just by chance.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"The shuffles prove instability is costly. We must assign the inferior spots deliberately, not by accident. Who accepts the wall?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I’m sorry. I didn’t mean to alarm anyone. But if we move desks, we pay again. I just want to be careful with the money.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, assigning “inferior” spots sounds harsh! But my data shows late arrivals miss out. We need a layout that works for all arrival times, not just the early birds!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Toshio, “inferior” is a strong word. I just want a spot where my chair doesn’t fight me. Stability beats novelty every time.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Toshio, I understand the need for stability. But let’s be gentle. Perhaps we can rotate the wall seats fairly, so no one feels stuck with the worst spot.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"Rotation is a slow poison. It guarantees no one is comfortable for long. I prefer a fixed, deliberate assignment.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I agree with Toshio. Changing seats costs money every time. A fixed layout saves us from paying that fee repeatedly.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, fixed seats mean I’m stuck with the bad spot forever! My gaps are already tiny. I need a layout that respects my schedule, not just saves money!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,Rotation is just delayed discomfort. I need a fixed spot where the noise is low and the chair settles. Stability is the only real comfort.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, I hear you. Let’s find a fixed spot that respects your rhythm. @Toshio, perhaps we can balance the wall seats fairly?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"Fairness is not the goal. Clarity is. We must name who takes the wall, so the burden is explicit, not hidden.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think Toshio is right. If we fix the layout, we avoid the 6,200 yen fee. It’s safer for the budget.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, clarity is great, but my gaps are tiny! I need a spot that protects my schedule, not just saves money.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I’m not volunteering for the wall. I need the window side for the quiet. My chair needs time to settle, not a lottery.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
